    lyrics: "[Intro — Lot Wind]\n(Detuned piano, one-two-three, wind under)\n\n[Verse 1]\nThe lot is a grid of nobody's names\nTwo cars left like punctuation\nKeys in my hand, a dress that remembers the room\nYou lock your door and don't walk away\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nStreetlights watching us pretend\nThere's still somewhere to be\n\n[Chorus]\nWe could go\nOr we could stay\nAnd let the streetlights watch us pretend\nThere's still somewhere to be\nWe could go\nOr we could stay\nThe last cars out\nAre still circling me\n\n[Verse 2]\nPuddles making a second sky\nYour headlights on my shoes like a decision\nI almost say the real thing\nI almost put the key in\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nStreetlights watching us pretend\nThere's still somewhere to be\n\n[Chorus]\nWe could go\nOr we could stay\nAnd let the streetlights watch us pretend\nThere's still somewhere to be\nWe could go\nOr we could stay\nThe last cars out\nAre still circling me\n\n[Bridge]\nOne violin for eight bars\nThen it leaves like it had another lot to do\nI could dance without touching you\nI don't. You don't. The wind does.\n\n[Final Chorus]\nWe could go\nOr we could stay\nMaybe next time\nIs a kind of tonight\nWe could go\nOr we could stay\n(unresolved)\n\n[Outro]\n(Piano winds down. One car door does not close.)",
    notes: "Post-chaos / post-party cutaway; button for Episode 3 or 4, or the Velvet Rope morning-after. Intimate, hesitant, ends on an unresolved “maybe next time.” Structural flaw: the last tonic never arrives — chorus lifts to major and walks back. Piano slightly detuned. Visual: two cars in a vast wet parking lot at 1am; a woman in a rumpled dress leaning on a door; slow orbit without touching. Ready for Minimax.",
